  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x2" flags="0x0">
    <title>B1 - Bypass target position transition step limit</title>
    <description>Step limit passed with new target and previous E3C4 to BD1E8 during state exit transition. Evidence: CPU E361E..E3640 applies cal1217 through BD1E8 while FD6A.2=1 and FD22.12=0. Confidence: structure transferred from M10062; target program unavailable Source image: 200kompressor_EVO_Nico_Tuned.BIN. Calibration block 1. FD22.12=0 and FD6A.2=1. Second motorized air flap: actual E3A2, target E3C4, motor PW3; distinct from main throttle E5EA/PW2. Bypass/recirculation identification is strongly supported by the air-path calculation and two-actuator architecture, but no verified physical connector-to-RAM or manufacturer symbol has been recovered. Position values remain native sensor counts, not degrees or percent. Native position units per invocation; execution interval unresolved.</description>
