  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x4" flags="0x0">
    <title>B1 - Air-path model speed ratio</title>
    <description>Converts engine speed to scaled model speed C9E4 used by model F7A6 and related air-path maps. Evidence: CPU CAFF6..CB006 shifts RPM and cal1702 left3 then BCDE4 returns product highword: C9E4=floor(RPM*cal9702/1024). Confidence: structure transferred from M10062; target program unavailable Source image: 200kompressor_EVO_Nico_Tuned.BIN. Calibration block 1. Equivalent formula assumes both shifted operands fit u16, as in normal calibrated range. Physical interpretation as supercharger shaft ratio strongly suggested, not confirmed by manufacturer symbols.</description>
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="-32" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>Index</units>
      <indexcount>1</indexcount>
