  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x69" flags="0x0">
    <title>B1 - State-dependent RPM limit - D06F threshold</title>
    <description>Upper engine speed cap. The lowest enabled cap becomes the active limit. Evidence: CPU DCACA..DCB8D takes the minimum of enabled byte caps; DCB82..DCB86 shifts left 5 and stores active limit E36A. Confidence: structure transferred from M10062; target program unavailable Source image: 200kompressor_EVO_Nico_Tuned.BIN. Calibration block 1. FD2C.3=1 and FD08.3=1 and D06F &gt; cal9344. State flags are named by their exact RAM bit. Manual/automatic, neutral and clutch labels are not proven for FD2C.3/FD78.5/E040/E041. D06F has not been identified; it must not be confused with coolant byte E06F.</description>
