  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x7d" flags="0x0">
    <title>B2 - Bypass demand filter gain - alternate branch</title>
    <description>Per-update first-order gain filtering calculated demand E3CA toward E3C8. Larger gain responds faster; it is not a position percentage. Evidence: CPU E35A4..E3602: select curve33EA/33F2, gain&lt;&lt;8, BCf54 filter, store E3C8. Confidence: structure transferred from M10062; target program unavailable Source image: 200kompressor_EVO_Nico_Tuned.BIN. Calibration block 2. FD22.12=1, FD88.0=1, FD6A.5=0. Second motorized air flap: actual E3A2, target E3C4, motor PW3; distinct from main throttle E5EA/PW2. Bypass/recirculation identification is strongly supported by the air-path calculation and two-actuator architecture, but no verified physical connector-to-RAM or manufacturer symbol has been recovered. Position values remain native sensor counts, not degrees or percent. Sampling period not established; % is fraction of remaining error per update, not seconds.</description>
