  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xf3" flags="0x0">
    <title>B3 - Bypass intervention - combined ignition correction threshold</title>
    <description>Threshold of combined ignition correction D098. If current correction is below the map value (more retard), the code accumulates positive E3DC and adds it to the second-flap target. Evidence: CPU E3382..E33DC: D098=D168+E00B+CEB6; axes1E8E/1E93 and table38C2; E3DC=clamp(E3DC+((map-D098)*cal1216 &gt;&gt;7),0,cal1712). E361A adds E3DC to flap position. Confidence: structure transferred from M10062; target program unavailable Source image: 200kompressor_EVO_Nico_Tuned.BIN. Calibration block 3. Second motorized air flap: actual E3A2, target E3C4, motor PW3; distinct from main throttle E5EA/PW2. Bypass/recirculation identification is strongly supported by the air-path calculation and two-actuator architecture, but no verified physical connector-to-RAM or manufacturer symbol has been recovered. Position values remain native sensor counts, not degrees or percent. Nominal angle scale is relative to neutral raw128; this is aggregate correction, not absolute BTDC or individual-cylinder knock retard.</description>
