  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x15f" flags="0x0">
    <title>B3 - Supercharger upper pressure ratio diagnosis threshold</title>
    <description>Maximum modeled supercharger pressure ratio versus engine speed. A sustained excess confirmed by diagnosis selects the bypass fallback position. Evidence: CPU CB406..CB444: interpolate pointer834F (DPP2=23 -&gt; fileC34F), compare E2D6 &gt; (lookup &lt;&lt;8), qualify through D30D0 and latch FD30.6. CB4A0..CB4A4 combines FD30.5/6 into FD30.4; E32FA..E3330 selects fallback cal971E. Confidence: structure transferred from M10062; target program unavailable Source image: 200kompressor_EVO_Nico_Tuned.BIN. Calibration block 3. Monitor enabled with FD12.8 set and FD2A.5, FD52.9, FD30.4 and FD22.12 clear. Ratio = raw/64, not bar or gauge boost. The upper monitor uses modeled E2D6, approximately 16384*E2BE/E2C8, rather than direct measured MAP/ambient pressure. Diagnostic qualification time in seconds, complete latch-reset conditions and exact DTC mapping are not established.</description>
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x0" mmedaddress="0x1809a" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedcolcount="8" mmedmajorstridebits="8" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>Engine speed (rpm)</units>
      <indexcount>8</indexcount>
      <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
      <outputtype>1</outputtype>
